A||||3||Frank Sombers||2.5 value adjustment?||||1||
Z||000000||Frank Sombers||04-06-2001||10:08 AM||||I have an '88 cpe with a 2.5 duke. It has 48,000 original miles, burns no oil, and runs strong. The engine (to me) seems to make a lot of noise. Not ever owning a car with a duke before I'm not sure if this is normal or not. The exhaust is not broken or leaking, and I changed to Mobil 1 synthetic (5-30) recently.<BR>My question is could the valves be in need adjustment? and can the valves even be adjusted?? I have been told by local "experts" that no they can't and yes they can. I would like to hear from people with first hand experience.<BR>Maybe I simply need to get used to the sound of the duke.<BR>Thanks<BR>Frank<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||ChadMan||04-06-2001||10:25 AM||||I doubt your valves are out of adjustment at 48K miles.  Dukes have noisy valvetrains by nature, but if you think your noise is excessive, check to see if your valve cover bolts have worked loose.<P>I noticed a lot of valvetrain noise from my 88 Coupe and found two valve cover bolts had loosened to the point of being finger-loose.  I tighted them down and it quieted down quite a bit.||||reg||10
Z||000002||84Bill||04-06-2001||01:06 PM||||Hey Frank<BR>I just recently aquired an 84 SE with (179,000) miles on it and I must say that it makes my 88 wit (97,000) miles sound like a 747 under full power. For some reason unknown to me my 88 just clatters unghodly. I've had it for almost 5 years and I guess I just got used to the rackett it makes. Since I got this 84 I can't hardly stand the 88 anymore. I did take the rear panel out of my 84 to remove some 3 pounds of extra wire (apparently they made a rolling concert speaker out of the car) the previous owner installed but notice no difference in the insulation. The only thing I can think of is the fact that GM changed the design of the engine, engine cradel and mounts this might account for the added noise both inside the car and out.<P>Bill||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||04-06-2001||08:19 PM||||There is something about the early DIS motor head that seems to make the valves noisy. I have some suspisions but I don't know for sure what it is.<P>As for noise/vibration inside the car.... check the motor mount. The mount only last so long reguardless of milage.<P>If the mount is bad replace it. Use the "liquid filled" one. make a peice of tin or aluminum for a shield over the top to keep oil out of it. Oil runs down the engine bracket and can collect on top of the mount afet oil filter changes. The oil helps kill the mount. A simple tin shield prevents that.||||reg||1
